1. The Janus Ledger

Two faces, one wall between them:

\boxed{
\text{PROMETHEUS}
\;|\;
\text{JANUS GATE}
\;|\;
\text{EPIMETHEUS}
}

Prometheus Book sees only information actually available at prediction time. This is where our real score comes from.

Epimetheus Book gets to cheat shamelessly. It knows which stocks won, constructs the portfolio afterward, then works backward asking why those winners won.

The Janus Gate permits patterns to cross from Epimetheus to Prometheus, but not future information:

\text{hindsight winner}
\rightarrow
\text{postmortem}
\rightarrow
\text{candidate invariant}
\rightarrow
\boxed{\text{LOOKAHEAD-TAINTED}}
\rightarrow
\text{forward test}

Only after it works prospectively does the taint come off.

That solves the biggest danger in your trick: hindsight explanation is extremely good at making accidents look inevitable.

