4. Why did the cheater win?

TEAM — Expectation Gap + Narrative Confirmation

Atlassian subsequently reported revenue of $1.8B, up 28%, cloud revenue up 31%, subscription ARR up 23%, and RPO up 44%. Its AI products were simultaneously reinforcing the growth narrative. 

Pattern:

\boxed{
\text{strong existing narrative}
+
\text{hard evidence}
+
\text{expectation beat}
+
\text{forward confirmation}
}

Not simply “good company.”

The price moves violently when reality upgrades faster than expectations.

⸻

SMCI — Bottleneck + Operating Inflection

Supermicro reported more than $60B in new orders, record backlog, greatly improved margins, and FY2027 revenue guidance of $65–72B against a prior analyst average around $52.5B. 

That’s another form of:

\text{expected future}
\ll
\text{newly revealed future}

But the underlying mechanism differs from TEAM:

AI\ demand
\rightarrow
\text{physical deployment bottleneck}
\rightarrow
\text{server demand}

That’s our AI Physicalization pattern.

