5. The first five Goblin Pattern Cards

We’ve therefore extracted five candidate signals from one cheating exercise:

\boxed{\textbf{Expectation Gap}}

Price can move violently when newly revealed reality exceeds the market’s prior model, not merely when fundamentals are good.

\boxed{\textbf{Probability Collapse}}

Uncertainty resolving favorably can create discontinuous repricing.

\boxed{\textbf{Bottleneck Migration}}

A system shock moves scarcity and pricing power to another node.

\boxed{\textbf{Policy-Backed Scarcity}}

Scarcity becomes much more valuable when a powerful buyer/regulator structurally supports demand.

\boxed{\textbf{Physicalization}}

A digital megatrend eventually creates unavoidable physical requirements—power, cooling, servers, land, construction, materials.

All five are currently stamped:

LOOKAHEAD-TAINTED — NOT YET PROVEN AS FORWARD EDGE

That’s essential.

