7. Pattern sharpening by subtraction

Suppose 100 historical winners share:

A+B+C+D

but 500 losers also share:

A+B+C

Then perhaps:

D

is the actual edge.

That’s Semantic Diff applied to investing.

\boxed{
\text{winning pattern}
-
\text{false friend}
=
\text{more precise invariant}
}

This is substantially better than ordinary “study successful stocks.”

Study successful stocks against things that looked almost identical and failed.

That’s how we learn what actually mattered.

